2:T452,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Trauma-Informed Classroom Management: Co-Regulation & The 2×10 Strategy","description":"Discover science-backed trauma-informed classroom management techniques: how co-regulation, the 2x10 strategy, and private repair reduce classroom disruptions by up to 85%.","datePublished":"2026-11-20","dateModified":"2026-11-24","articleSection":"Educators","keywords":"trauma-informed classroom management, co-regulation in the classroom, 2x10 strategy teaching, de-escalating dysregulated students, teacher burnout nervous system regulation, restorative classroom discipline, neuroception of safety in schools","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://vibehyr.com/blog/trauma-informed-classroom-co-regulation-2x10-strategy"},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Keisha Solomon","jobTitle":"Founder & Master Architect, Vibe Hyr"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe Hyr","url":"https://vibehyr.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://vibehyr.com/icons/icon-512.png"}},"image":"https://vibehyr.com/images/og-image.png"}3:T5ea,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is co-regulation in the classroom?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Co-regulation is the biological process by which a calm, regulated adult nervous system lends stability to a dysregulated student's nervous system through vocal tone, non-threatening posture, predictable routines, and relational safety. Because mirror neurons and neuroception operate below conscious thought, co-regulation must happen before cognitive instruction or behavioral reflection can work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the 2×10 strategy work for challenging students?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The 2×10 strategy requires spending 2 minutes per day for 10 consecutive school days having a genuine 1-on-1 conversation with a high-friction student about anything unrelated to behavior, grades, or compliance. This builds a relational \"trust deposit\" so future redirections are received as support rather than threat."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you hold students accountable without public shaming?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use the principle of \"dignity in public, accountability in private.\" Interrupt unsafe or disruptive behavior calmly using proximity and the Low-Slow-Sideways stance, defer the deeper consequence conversation until the student's prefrontal cortex is back online, and conduct the 3-Step Private Repair Protocol away from the peer audience."}}]}8:["slug","trauma-informed-classroom-co-regulation-2x10-strategy","d"]
0:["A6jreOC79KKPZRtx9TnSh",[[["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","trauma-informed-classroom-co-regulation-2x10-strategy","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"trauma-informed-classroom-co-regulation-2x10-strategy\"}",{}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","trauma-informed-classroom-co-regulation-2x10-strategy","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://vibehyr.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Blog\",\"item\":\"https://vibehyr.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Trauma-Informed Classroom Management: Co-Regulation & The 2×10 Strategy That Cuts Disruptions\",\"item\":\"https://vibehyr.com/blog/trauma-informed-classroom-co-regulation-2x10-strategy\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$3"}}],["$","$L4",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"pt-[68px] min-h-screen","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"py-14 px-6 md:px-14 border-b border-white/8 relative","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-1 bg-orange-DEFAULT"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto pl-4","children":[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"mb-8","children":["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-grey-dark flex-wrap","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L5",null,{"href":"/","className":"hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors","children":"Home"}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L5",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors","children":"Blog"}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","li",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT truncate max-w-xs","aria-current":"page","children":"Educators"}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap mb-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.55rem] tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT","children":"Educators"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.48rem] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase px-2.5 py-0.5 bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 text-grey-DEFAULT","children":"Educators"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-[0.55rem] tracking-[0.1em] text-grey-dark","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":10,"height":10,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-clock","children":[["$","circle","1mglay",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"}],["$","polyline","68esgv",{"points":"12 6 12 12 16 14"}],"$undefined"]}]," ",10," min read"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"font-display text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem)] leading-[0.95] tracking-[0.02em] text-white mb-5","children":"Trauma-Informed Classroom Management: Co-Regulation & The 2×10 Strategy That Cuts Disruptions"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body italic text-grey-DEFAULT text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6","children":"Public consequences and power struggles trigger adolescent social threat and escalate classroom disruptions. Discover how Zone 2 somatic room-reading, the 2×10 relational strategy, and private repair transform classroom culture."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4 pt-5 border-t border-white/10 font-mono text-[0.5rem] tracking-widest text-grey-dark","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":["By ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white font-medium","children":"Keisha Solomon"}]," · ","Founder & Master Architect, Vibe Hyr"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["Published ",["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-11-20","children":"November 19, 2026"}]]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[#dfbd8b]","children":["Updated ",["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-11-24","children":"November 23, 2026"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-12 px-6 md:px-14","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto","children":[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Table of Contents","className":"mb-10 p-6 bg-black-2 border border-orange-DEFAULT/25","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT mb-3","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":13,"height":13,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-book-open","children":[["$","path","vv98re",{"d":"M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"}],["$","path","1cyq3y",{"d":"M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"}],"$undefined"]}],"In This Guide"]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-2","children":[["$","li","why-traditional-classroom-discipline-backfires-on-dysregulated-brains",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#why-traditional-classroom-discipline-backfires-on-dysregulated-brains","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["01","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Why Traditional Classroom Discipline Backfires on Dysregulated Brains"}]]}]}],["$","li","the-educators-nervous-system-is-the-classroom-intervention",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-educators-nervous-system-is-the-classroom-intervention","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["02","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Educator's Nervous System Is the Classroom Intervention"}]]}]}],["$","li","catching-dysregulation-at-the-whisper-stage",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#catching-dysregulation-at-the-whisper-stage","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["03","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Catching Dysregulation at the \"Whisper Stage\""}]]}]}],["$","li","the-210-relational-strategy-an-85-reduction-in-disruptions",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-210-relational-strategy-an-85-reduction-in-disruptions","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["04","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The 2×10 Relational Strategy: An 85% Reduction in Disruptions"}]]}]}],["$","li","dignity-in-public-accountability-in-private",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#dignity-in-public-accountability-in-private","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["05","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Dignity in Public, Accountability in Private"}]]}]}]]}]]}],[["$","h2","0",{"id":"why-traditional-classroom-discipline-backfires-on-dysregulated-brains","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"Why Traditional Classroom Discipline Backfires on Dysregulated Brains"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Every educator knows the moment: a student slams a chromebook shut, mutters under their breath, or refuses to open their packet. The traditional compliance model says to assert immediate public authority — call their name across the room, issue a warning, or threaten a consequence."]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["And almost every time, the student doubles down."]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Here is the neurobiological reason why: during adolescence, the brain's social-threat circuitry is hyper-sensitized. Being corrected or embarrassed in front of peers triggers an ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"amygdala hijack"}]," identical to physical danger. Once a student enters fight-or-flight (Zone 3 or Zone 4), blood flow shifts away from the prefrontal cortex — the very part of the brain required to weigh consequences, regulate impulses, or comply with verbal lectures."]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"You cannot lecture a brain that has gone offline."}]," Co-regulation must precede cognition."]}],["$","h2","5",{"id":"the-educators-nervous-system-is-the-classroom-intervention","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The Educator's Nervous System Is the Classroom Intervention"}],["$","p","6",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["In the Vibe Hyr Educators curriculum (",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"Program 01: The Educator Reset"}]," and ",["$","em","3",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"Program 03: Co-Regulation Mastery"}],"), we begin with an uncomfortable truth: ",["$","strong","5",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"dysregulation is contagious, design-wise, in both directions."}],""]}],["$","p","7",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Through mirror neurons and what Dr. Stephen Porges calls ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"neuroception"}]," (the nervous system's subconscious scanning for cues of safety or threat), 28 students read your muscular tension, breathing rate, and vocal micro-tremors within five seconds of walking through your door."]}],["$","h3","8",{"className":"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl tracking-[0.03em] text-orange-DEFAULT mt-8 mb-3","children":"The 30-Second Threshold Reset"}],["$","p","9",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Before unlocking your classroom door for your most challenging period:"]}],["$","ol","10",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-3 my-6","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-orange-DEFAULT text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["01","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Physical Anchor:"}]," Place your hand on the door handle and take two physiological sighs (double inhale through the nose, long slow exhale through the mouth)."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-orange-DEFAULT text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["02","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Assumption Revision:"}]," Notice if you are bracing for battle (",["$","em","3",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"\"4th period is always a nightmare\""}],"). Replace that predictive filter with an intentional assumption: ",["$","em","5",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"\"My regulated presence anchors this room. These students borrow my calm.\""}],""]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-orange-DEFAULT text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["03","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Zone 2 Entry:"}]," Greet students at the threshold with a warm, unhurried cadence."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2","11",{"id":"catching-dysregulation-at-the-whisper-stage","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"Catching Dysregulation at the \"Whisper Stage\""}],["$","p","12",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Classroom explosions rarely happen out of nowhere. Every student broadcasts early somatic \"whispers\" 3 to 5 minutes before a behavioral shout:"]}],["$","ul","13",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-3 my-6","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Rapid foot-tapping or pencil snapping"]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Hood pulled tightly over the eyes or head dropped to the desk"]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Sudden silence from a usually talkative student"]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Scanning the room for peer reactions"]}]]}]]}],["$","p","14",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["When you catch dysregulation at the whisper stage, you never need a public showdown. Walk over casually, stand ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"sideways"}]," rather than towering face-to-face (",["$","strong","3",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Low, Slow, and Sideways"}],"), and offer a quiet 10-second check-in or a regulatory off-ramp (a water break, a choice of where to start, or a silent visual cue)."]}],["$","h2","15",{"id":"the-210-relational-strategy-an-85-reduction-in-disruptions","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The 2×10 Relational Strategy: An 85% Reduction in Disruptions"}],["$","p","16",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The highest-leverage proactive tool in trauma-informed teaching is the ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"2×10 Strategy"}],":"]}],["$","ul","17",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-3 my-6","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Identify the ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"one or two students"}]," who generate 80% of the classroom friction."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Commit to ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"2 minutes per day for 10 consecutive school days"}]," of 1-on-1 conversation with that student about ",["$","em","3",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"anything except academics or behavior"}]," — music, sneakers, video games, sports, weekend plans."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-grey-DEFAULT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT mt-1 flex-shrink-0","children":"✦"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Make zero behavioral demands during those two minutes."]}]]}]]}],["$","p","18",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Why does this produce up to an 85% drop in referrals within two weeks? Because a student's brain categorizes adults into two buckets: ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Allies"}]," and ",["$","strong","3",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"Adversaries"}],". When a student has ten consecutive days of non-transactional warmth deposited in their nervous system, a redirection on Day 11 is processed by their brain as ",["$","em","5",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"coaching from an ally"}]," rather than ",["$","em","7",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"an attack from an adversary"}],"."]}],["$","h2","19",{"id":"dignity-in-public-accountability-in-private","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"Dignity in Public, Accountability in Private"}],["$","p","20",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["When a boundary is crossed and other students watch to see what you will do, avoid the trap of performative punishment. Use this one-sentence anchor with the class:"]}],["$","blockquote","21",{"className":"border-l-2 border-orange-DEFAULT pl-6 my-8 font-body italic text-grey-DEFAULT text-lg leading-relaxed","children":["",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"\"In this room, everyone gets dignity in public and accountability in private — including you if you ever have a hard day.\""}],""]}],["$","p","22",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["When students learn that your classroom protects their dignity even on their worst day, power struggles evaporate and genuine accountability takes root."]}]],["$","section",null,{"aria-labelledby":"faq-heading","className":"mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-white/10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT mb-2","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":13,"height":13,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle-help","children":[["$","circle","1mglay",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"}],["$","path","1u773s",{"d":"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"}],["$","path","p32p05",{"d":"M12 17h.01"}],"$undefined"]}],"Key Questions Answered"]}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"faq-heading","className":"font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mb-6","children":"FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"bg-black-2 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:border-orange-DEFAULT/30 transition-colors","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-body font-semibold text-white text-base mb-2","children":"What is co-regulation in the classroom?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"Co-regulation is the biological process by which a calm, regulated adult nervous system lends stability to a dysregulated student's nervous system through vocal tone, non-threatening posture, predictable routines, and relational safety. Because mirror neurons and neuroception operate below conscious thought, co-regulation must happen before cognitive instruction or behavioral reflection can work."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"bg-black-2 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:border-orange-DEFAULT/30 transition-colors","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-body font-semibold text-white text-base mb-2","children":"How does the 2×10 strategy work for challenging students?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"The 2×10 strategy requires spending 2 minutes per day for 10 consecutive school days having a genuine 1-on-1 conversation with a high-friction student about anything unrelated to behavior, grades, or compliance. This builds a relational \"trust deposit\" so future redirections are received as support rather than threat."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"bg-black-2 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:border-orange-DEFAULT/30 transition-colors","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-body font-semibold text-white text-base mb-2","children":"How do you hold students accountable without public shaming?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"Use the principle of \"dignity in public, accountability in private.\" Interrupt unsafe or disruptive behavior calmly using proximity and the Low-Slow-Sideways stance, defer the deeper consequence conversation until the student's prefrontal cortex is back online, and conduct the 3-Step Private Repair Protocol away from the peer audience."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-white/8 flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.48rem] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-grey-dark mr-2","children":"Topics:"}],[["$","s